ue" data-input-selector-label-measure="true" class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 h-0 w-max max-w-none overflow-hidden text-sm leading-5 whitespace-nowrap opacity-0 [&amp;_.katex]:!text-[1em]"><span class="katex"><span class="katex"><span class="katex-mathml"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class="katex-html" aria-hidden="true"><span class="base"><span class="strut" style="height:0.6833em;"></span><span class="mord mathnormal" style="margin-right:0.00773em;">R</span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div></div><div class="sr-only">Source voltage in volts drives the same loop current through the whole one-resistor circuit, and resistance in ohms limits that current, using Ohm's law. The interactive controls focus on a teaching-friendly range and can expand for seeded examples. The resistor's inner pipe narrows as a visual cue for higher resistance, not as a literal mechanical clamp. The blue arrow and resistor markers are qualitative conventional current cues, not microscopic charge-speed measurements. In this one-resistor model, the source voltage equals the resistor voltage drop; heating, power limits, and non-ohmic behavior are not shown.</div></div></div></div></div><div class="AxvpHG_visualizationLayer -m-3 relative min-w-0 flex-1 place-items-center overflow-hidden border-t @md:border-s @md:border-t-0 border-token-border-default"><div aria-hidden="true" class="bg-token-bg-primary pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 z-0 dark:bg-[#2a2a2a]"></div><div class="relative z-1 flex place-items-center size-full"><svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 260 220" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" role="img" aria-label="Ohm&#39;s law visualization for an ideal ohmic resistor in a one-resistor circuit with a variable DC source. Current I is 2 amperes everywhere in the loop. Resistance R is 6 ohms. Source voltage is 12 volts. The resistor&#39;s inner pipe narrows as a visual cue for higher resistance, not as a literal clamp. The blue arrow and resistor markers show relative conventional current." class="h-auto w-full" style="aspect-ratio: 260 / 220;"><g fill="none" stroke="var(--text-secondary)" stroke-linecap="butt" stroke-linejoin="round" opacity="0.62"><path d="M 41 95 L 41 78 L 92 78" stroke-width="2.4"></path><path d="M 184 78 L 226 78 L 226 170 L 41 170 L 41 159" stroke-width="2.4"></path></g><rect x="34" y="95" width="14" height="6" rx="1.5" fill="var(--text-primary)" opacity="0.78"></rect><rect x="24" y="101" width="34" height="58" rx="5" fill="var(--bg-secondary)" stroke="var(--text-primary)" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.9"></rect><text x="14" y="64" fill="var(--text-secondary)" font-size="8" text-anchor="start" style="font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;"><tspan>V</tspan><tspan baseline-shift="sub" font-size="5.6">s</tspan><tspan> = 12.0 V</tspan></text><text x="41" y="120" fill="var(--text-primary)" font-size="10" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" opacity="1">+</text><text x="41" y="147" fill="var(--text-primary)" font-size="10" font-weight="600" text-anchor="middle" opacity="1">-</text><rect x="92" y="61" width="92" height="34" rx="4" fill="var(--bg-secondary)" stroke="var(--border-heavy)" stroke-width="1.4"></rect><path d="M 100 69.5 C 118 69.5 120 70.88205128205128 138 70.88205128205128 C 156 70.88205128205128 158 69.5 176 69.5 L 176 86.5 C 158 86.5 156 85.11794871794872 138 85.11794871794872 C 120 85.11794871794872 118 86.5 100 86.5 Z" fill="var(--learning-block-accent)" fill-opacity="0.04" stroke="var(--text-secondary)" stroke-opacity="0.21384615384615385" stroke-width="0.9"></path><g><circle cx="103.4857738033247" cy="78" r="1.485773803324704" fill="var(--learning-block-accent)" opacity="0.47678400846904057"><animate attributeName="cx" values="103.4857738033247;172.5142261966753" dur="2.38s" begin="-0.00s" repeatCount="indefinite"></animate></circle><circle cx="